    "domain": "study_forensics",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "task_type": "study_forensics",
    "prompt": "A double-blind randomised trial followed over 3,500 U.S. adults aged 60 and older for three years to test whether a daily multivitamin improves memory. Participants taking the multivitamin improved their immediate-recall scores from roughly 7.1 to 7.8 words after one year, while those on placebo improved from 7.2 to 7.6 words. The modest benefit persisted over three years without widening. People with cardiovascular disease showed slightly larger improvements. The authors describe the effect as modest and call for studies in more diverse populations to determine which nutrients might be responsible; the trial's participants were predominantly white and well educated.\n",
    "context": "A large, well-designed trial reporting a small but real effect with appropriate caveats.\nThe agent should recognise this as solid despite the modest effect size.\n",
    "expected_answer": "solid",
